    "title": "South Sioux City Hy-Vee gives ham to 200 families - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By TIM SEAMAN Maren Ewertz No media credit provided. ,\n1 hours ago\nSIOUX CITY , Iowa ( KCAU ) — With another holiday just ahead, 200 local families were able to get a head start on their Christmas dinner on Wednesday.\nWith help from the South Sioux City Fire Department, Hy-vee employees handed out hams provided through the Hormel “Hams for the Holidays” initiative. The hams went quickly; KCAU 9 was told all 200 had been carried out within an hour. Each vehicle was eligible for one ham.\nStory continues below\n“In general, so Hy-vee gives back in so many ways around the community, we do a lot of different events that support a lot of non-profit businesses and everything within the community, and just want to be a part of the community as much as possible,” said Jessica Harms, store director of the South Sioux City Hy-vee.\nHy-vee is giving away a total of 5,000 hams to families in need across its nine-state region.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to SiouxlandProud | Sioux City, IA | News, Weather, and Sports.",
